**Description**

This program is an interactive soccer simulation game where the user competes against the computer in a 90-play match, with each play representing a minute of game time. At the start, the user selects their team and an opponent from a list of top international soccer clubs, which will be presented through a graphical interface built with Tkinter. Each team consists of 11 players, and the user controls one player at a time. During the gameplay, the user can choose offensive actions such as dribbling, passing, or shooting, or opt for defense. The success of each action depends on whether the user answers a soccer-themed trivia question correctly. The game outputs the animated plays and a final score  using Tkinter’s Canvas. To promote accessibility, the application includes an option to switch to a dyslexia-friendly font and the start screen incorporates a music which includes voiceover of the title "Welcome to the Soccer Game". 

This program needs the tkinter, PIL, os, random, sys, and pygame modules to be imported.

**Execution**

To run the program, download the file Final_PY_DuSivasankarXiu.py, the image "Final_mainIMG_DuSivasankarXiu.png", the gif "Final_shootsuccessGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif," the gif "Final_shootfailGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif," the gif "Final_passsuccessGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif", the gif "Final_passfailGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif", the gif "Final_dribblesuccessGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif," the gif "Final_dribblefailGIF_DuSivasankarXiu.gif," and the music "Final_mainIMG_DuSivasankarXiu". Place all of these files in one folder and name the folder "FinalProject11". In addition, install Pillow and Pygame on your computer by going to terminal and enter "pip install Pillow" and "pip install pygame" (or pip3 install Pilow and pip3 install pygame). Also download Dyslexic Font from https://opendyslexic.org and upload the font into your computer. 

Run the program through the terminal and view the tkinter window screens to play the game.

